{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-69661" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If\n$S=[\\begin{aligned}1-p & 1+p \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]$\nand $det(S)=2$, what is the value of $p?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974230/state.json" "file_sha256" "4932842abe34174cc0d901d67cbbda90d7bc99e2eae7366d1854020007f08002"} {"question" "q-69661" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(S) & =|\\begin{aligned}1-p & 1+p \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(1-p)\\cdot 2-(1+p)\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =2-2p+3+3p \\\\  & =5+p\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(S)=2$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(S) & =2 \\\\ 5+p & =2 \\\\ p & =2-5 \\\\ p & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974230/state.json" "file_sha256" "4932842abe34174cc0d901d67cbbda90d7bc99e2eae7366d1854020007f08002"} {"question" "q-69661" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974230/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0510e57de7a3782588cfbae83eceaa161c665c939346a0623bb1b74a9cd49b39"} {"question" "q-69661" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974230/state.json" "file_sha256" "4932842abe34174cc0d901d67cbbda90d7bc99e2eae7366d1854020007f08002"} {"question" "q-69661" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-3"] ["math" "-6"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974230/state.json" "file_sha256" "4932842abe34174cc0d901d67cbbda90d7bc99e2eae7366d1854020007f08002"} {"question" "q-69661" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974230/state.json" "file_sha256" "4932842abe34174cc0d901d67cbbda90d7bc99e2eae7366d1854020007f08002"} {"question" "q-127601" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $det(C)$, if\n    $C=[\\begin{aligned}-x & -2y \\\\ \\frac{x}{2} & 5y\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974230/state.json" "file_sha256" "4932842abe34174cc0d901d67cbbda90d7bc99e2eae7366d1854020007f08002"} {"question" "q-127601" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(C) & =|\\begin{aligned}-x & -2y \\\\ \\frac{x}{2} & 5y\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-x\\cdot 5y-(-2y)\\cdot \\frac{x}{2} \\\\  & =-5xy+xy \\\\  & =-4xy\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974230/state.json" "file_sha256" "4932842abe34174cc0d901d67cbbda90d7bc99e2eae7366d1854020007f08002"} {"question" "q-127601" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974230/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0510e57de7a3782588cfbae83eceaa161c665c939346a0623bb1b74a9cd49b39"} {"question" "q-127601" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974230/state.json" "file_sha256" "4932842abe34174cc0d901d67cbbda90d7bc99e2eae7366d1854020007f08002"} {"question" "q-127601" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-4xy"] ["math" "-5xy"] ["math" "-\\frac{3xy}{2}"] ["math" "5xy"] ["math" "\\frac{5xy}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974230/state.json" "file_sha256" "4932842abe34174cc0d901d67cbbda90d7bc99e2eae7366d1854020007f08002"} {"question" "q-127601" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-4xy"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974230/state.json" "file_sha256" "4932842abe34174cc0d901d67cbbda90d7bc99e2eae7366d1854020007f08002"} {"question" "q-127603" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $det(D)$, if\n    $D=[\\begin{aligned}2x & y \\\\ -5 & xy\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974230/state.json" "file_sha256" "4932842abe34174cc0d901d67cbbda90d7bc99e2eae7366d1854020007f08002"} {"question" "q-127603" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(D) & =|\\begin{aligned}2x & y \\\\ -5 & xy\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2x\\cdot xy-y\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}y+5y \\\\  & =y(2{x}^{2}+5)\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974230/state.json" "file_sha256" "4932842abe34174cc0d901d67cbbda90d7bc99e2eae7366d1854020007f08002"} {"question" "q-127603" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974230/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0510e57de7a3782588cfbae83eceaa161c665c939346a0623bb1b74a9cd49b39"} {"question" "q-127603" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974230/state.json" "file_sha256" "4932842abe34174cc0d901d67cbbda90d7bc99e2eae7366d1854020007f08002"} {"question" "q-127603" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3{x}^{2}y+3"] ["math" "3{y}^{2}x-5"] ["math" "4{x}^{2}{y}^{2}"] ["math" "y(2{x}^{2}+5)"] ["math" "y(2{x}^{2}-3)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974230/state.json" "file_sha256" "4932842abe34174cc0d901d67cbbda90d7bc99e2eae7366d1854020007f08002"} {"question" "q-127603" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y(2{x}^{2}+5)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974230/state.json" "file_sha256" "4932842abe34174cc0d901d67cbbda90d7bc99e2eae7366d1854020007f08002"} {"question" "q-127606" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If\n$T=[\\begin{aligned}v & 2v \\\\ 2 & v+8\\end{aligned}]$\nand $det(T)=-4$, what is the value of $v?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974230/state.json" "file_sha256" "4932842abe34174cc0d901d67cbbda90d7bc99e2eae7366d1854020007f08002"} {"question" "q-127606" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(T) & =|\\begin{aligned}v & 2v \\\\ 2 & v+8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =v\\cdot (v+8)-2v\\cdot 2 \\\\  & ={v}^{2}+4v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(T)=-4$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(T) & =-4 \\\\ {v}^{2}+4v & =-4 \\\\ {v}^{2}+4v+4 & =0 \\\\ (v+2)^{2} & =0 \\\\ v & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974230/state.json" "file_sha256" "4932842abe34174cc0d901d67cbbda90d7bc99e2eae7366d1854020007f08002"} {"question" "q-127606" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974230/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0510e57de7a3782588cfbae83eceaa161c665c939346a0623bb1b74a9cd49b39"} {"question" "q-127606" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974230/state.json" "file_sha256" "4932842abe34174cc0d901d67cbbda90d7bc99e2eae7366d1854020007f08002"} {"question" "q-127606" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "v=-2"] ["math" "v=-3"] ["math" "v=4"] ["math" "v=\\frac{3}{4}"] ["math" "v=\\frac{7}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974230/state.json" "file_sha256" "4932842abe34174cc0d901d67cbbda90d7bc99e2eae7366d1854020007f08002"} {"question" "q-127606" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "v=-2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974230/state.json" "file_sha256" "4932842abe34174cc0d901d67cbbda90d7bc99e2eae7366d1854020007f08002"} {"question" "q-317374" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the determinant:\n\n$|\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{6} & y \\\\ 4 & \\sqrt{6}\\end{aligned}|=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974230/state.json" "file_sha256" "4932842abe34174cc0d901d67cbbda90d7bc99e2eae7366d1854020007f08002"} {"question" "q-317374" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{6} & y \\\\ 4 & \\sqrt{6}\\end{aligned}| & =\\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\sqrt{6}-y\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =6-4y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974230/state.json" "file_sha256" "4932842abe34174cc0d901d67cbbda90d7bc99e2eae7366d1854020007f08002"} {"question" "q-317374" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974230/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0510e57de7a3782588cfbae83eceaa161c665c939346a0623bb1b74a9cd49b39"} {"question" "q-317374" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974230/state.json" "file_sha256" "4932842abe34174cc0d901d67cbbda90d7bc99e2eae7366d1854020007f08002"} {"question" "q-317374" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6-4y"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974230/state.json" "file_sha256" "4932842abe34174cc0d901d67cbbda90d7bc99e2eae7366d1854020007f08002"}] "usage" {} "basis" 710 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_